  "name": "athletics-qualifies-within-needs-a-finish",
  "why": "`qualifies_within` is a finish inside the time, not elapsed time inside it, and the finish is the place the rule is bound to — here the course’s one finish line. One runner finishes in 45:00 and qualifies, one finishes in 55:00 and does not, one withdraws at 6 km after 30:00 and one was last read at 5 km after 25:00. The last two are inside fifty minutes of elapsed time — which runs to the last read — and never reached the finish, so neither qualifies.",
